The message Cannot GET /account is an important clue.

It means Express never matched your route. Your route is:

app.get("/account/:email", ...)

This route requires an email after /account/.

For example:

GET https://your-render-app.onrender.com/account/test@gmail.com

or URL-encoded:

GET https://your-render-app.onrender.com/account/test%40gmail.com

If you're requesting only:

GET https://your-render-app.onrender.com/account

then Express will respond with:

Cannot GET /account

because there is no route for /account.

